  abstract = {Governance: A Very Short Introduction explains the main theories of governance and their impact in the corporate, public, and global spheres. The many uses of the term 'governance' are expolored: the World Bank and the International Monetary Fund make loans conditional on 'good governance'; climate change and avian flu appear as issues of 'global governance'; the US Forest Service calls for 'collaborative governance'. Why is the term used so pervasively and to what does it refer? What makes good or bad governance?}
}

@book{arnold2000history,
